<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 24,540,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 24,540,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 06/18/97    06/11/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 24,540,000  25,378,000    24,078,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  46,853	70,240	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   06/18/97    06/11/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,067,000   3,965,000     3,789,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,804,000   4,703,000     3,897,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,876,000   4,154,000     4,229,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,079,000   2,808,000     2,343,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,429,000   3,451,000     3,452,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,107,000   4,262,000     4,926,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,177,000   2,034,000     1,442,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	24,540,000  25,378,000    24,078,000</p>
